 C/CW:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/CW - write one character to the file whose FCB is in M12.
C
C   ACC = the character to write
C   M12 = the FILE record
C   M13 = return link
C
C The character is stored into the current element slot, f^,
C which FILE[0] addresses through the working tag, and C/PF
C then puts it and advances the file.  C/PF is entered by a
C jump, not a call, so it returns through M13 straight to our
C own caller.  C/7A open-codes this same three-instruction
C sequence in its inner loop rather than calling here.
C===========================================================
 C/PF:          ,SUBP,        . Put f^ and advance the file
                ,ntr , 3
            12  ,wtc ,        . Address f^ through FILE[0]
                ,atx ,        . f^ := the character
                ,uj  , C/PF   . Tail-call the writer
                ,end ,
